The tarball as it is supplied should be suitable for creating a distribution
package without major modification.

Please contact the author for any questions, suggestions or fixes, so they can be merged upstream:
remon at traverso-daw dot org


CPU features:

Nothing to set. The buffer operations of the audio path are built for the
baseline of the target and, on x86-64 with GCC or Clang, also for AVX2; the
CPU decides at run time which one runs (TCpuFeatures). Your distribution's
flags (CFLAGS, CXXFLAGS, e.g. -O2 from dpkg-buildflags) are used as they are.
32-bit x86 (i386, i686) is not supported; CMake stops with a message.
32-bit ARM is.

The old flags -DSSE_OPTIMIZATIONS, -DUSE_XMMINTRIN, -DARCH_X86 and the
options DETECT_HOST_CPU_FEATURES, WANT_SSE and USE_SYSTEM_SLV2_LIBRARY are
gone; passing them does nothing.


Features:

Audio drivers and plugins are CMake options (WANT_ALSA, WANT_JACK,
WANT_PIPEWIRE, WANT_PORTAUDIO, WANT_COREAUDIO, WANT_LV2, WANT_M4A_DECODE,
WANT_M4A_ENCODE); the defaults depend on the platform. AAC and MP4 are read by
FFmpeg 8.0 or newer, a required dependency; WANT_M4A_DECODE only builds the
FAAD reader, which nothing uses. E.g.:

cmake -S . -B build -DWANT_JACK=ON -DWANT_ALSA=ON -DWANT_PIPEWIRE=ON
